github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg-libs/windows_arm64
================================================

lib/ contains FFmpeg libraries (https://ffmpeg.org) built for windows_arm64:

  libavcodec.a libavdevice.a libavformat.a libavutil.a libgoffmpeg.dll libswresample.a libswscale.a

FFmpeg version: N-125841-ge2bc6d88cd (git revision e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a).
No local patches: goffmpeg's build applies patches/*.patch to the FFmpeg
checkout, and goffmpeg has no such files (BUILDING.md: "The directory is
currently empty").

License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. The full
text is in LICENSE at the root of this repository, and is included in this
module's zip by the go command. The build used neither --enable-gpl nor
--enable-nonfree; each library reports "license: LGPL version 2.1 or later".

lib/libgoffmpeg.dll is linked by llvm-mingw 20261006 and so
contains parts of the MinGW-w64 runtime (startup code and C runtime glue).
Some of it requires its copyright and license notices to accompany
binaries: they are in COPYING.MinGW-w64-runtime.txt in this module, taken
from mingw-w64's own copy of that file. The static libraries in lib/
contain no runtime code.
llvm-mingw's compiler-rt builtins are linked too, under Apache-2.0 WITH
LLVM-exception, which does not require a notice for compiled code.

Configure line, as recorded in libavutil (avutil_configuration()).

  --prefix=/windows_arm64 --extra-cflags=-fPIC --enable-pic --disable-autodetect --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-debug --disable-encoders --disable-muxers --disable-avfilter --enable-swscale --enable-swresample --enable-network --arch=aarch64 --target-os=mingw32 --enable-cross-compile --cross-prefix=/opt/llvm-mingw/bin/aarch64-w64-mingw32- --enable-schannel --enable-avdevice --enable-indev=dshow --enable-static --disable-shared

Corresponding source:
  FFmpeg:  https://github.com/belluikit/ffmpeg/tree/goffmpeg-e2bc6d88cd
           belluikit's mirror of FFmpeg. The tag is commit
           e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a and stays for as long as
           libraries built from it are published.
  Build:   https://github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg (Makefile, BUILDING.md), which
           pins that revision and this configure line.
  Bridge:  lib/libgoffmpeg.* is these FFmpeg libraries linked with goffmpeg's
           bridge.c (BSD-3-Clause), built by goffmpeg's 'make bridge-shared'.
           The current lib/libgoffmpeg.* was built from goffmpeg commit
           cc0758b by GitHub Actions run 40594708079, linked against FFmpeg
           libraries built in that same run: the lib/*.a in this module.
